<p class="c5"><span class="c10">GENERAL PROVISIONS</span></p>
<p class="c5"><span class="c0">When reasonable grounds concerning the performance of either party arise, the non-offending party may in writing demand adequate assurance of performance by the other by a notice in 18 point font, Times New Roman, as set forth below, delivered to the other party. The offending party&#39;s failure to provide within 10 days of demand, such assurance of performance as is adequate under the circumstances is a default under this Agreement.</span>
